## 🎬 SCENE 5: Video Composition (2:30 - 3:00)

### Screen
- Show Shotstack JSON Builder node
- Show HTTP Request to Shotstack API

### Narration (English)
```
"The generated media is composed into a final video 
using Shotstack API.

We add Korean subtitles, background music, 
and text-to-speech narration.

The final video is 50 seconds long in 9:16 vertical format,
perfect for YouTube Shorts."
```

---

## 🎬 SCENE 6: YouTube API Upload - THE KEY SECTION (3:00 - 4:00)

### Screen
- **ZOOM INTO** YouTube Upload node
- Show node configuration (blur OAuth tokens!)
- Show API endpoint being called

### Narration (English)
```
"Finally, we use the YouTube Data API to upload the video.

We ONLY use these API endpoints:
- videos.insert - to upload the video file
- videos.update - to set title, description, and tags

We do NOT scrape, download, or collect any user data.
We do NOT access any third-party channels.
We ONLY upload to our own managed channels."
```

### Key Points to Show
- OAuth2 credential (name only, blur tokens!)
- "videos.insert" visible in configuration
- Upload status: "private" or "public"

---

